{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbF1z389RobJLRmRgU2a", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_013qnkv2cqmrNnoBqynQtrvk", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes — serial divider + shared multiplier (cores/bench)\n\n## What changed\n\n- `rtl/divider.sv` (new): radix-2 restoring serial divider, one-hot FSM\n  IDLE -> PREP -> RUN(32) -> FIX -> DONE.\n  - IDLE+`start` latches the raw post-forwarding `a`/`b` plus `is_signed`/`want_rem`\n    into `a_q`/`b_q`/flags (no negation, so the forwarding path is not lengthened).\n  - PREP computes |a|, |b|, clears the remainder, records `neg_q`/`neg_r`.\n    `neg_q` is suppressed when b == 0, so signed DIV by 0 stays all-ones.\n  - RUN: 33-bit shifted remainder `{rem, quo[31]}` vs |b| through one 34-bit\n    subtract; borrow selects restore/keep. (The hypothesis text wrote\n    `rem = {rem[30:0], q[31]}`; that would drop the top bit when |b| > 2^31, so\n    the shifted value is 33 bits wide and `rem` is 32 bits.)\n  - FIX: single shared negate of the selected (quotient|remainder) -> `quo` register.\n  - DONE: `done=1`, `result=quo`. Back to IDLE when `advance` (= `!stall_ex_mem`).\n  - 35 busy cycles + the DONE cycle per divide.\n  - Whole FSM under `ifndef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`; ALTOPS ties done/result/a_q/b_q to 0.\n  - Interface deviation: no `busy` output (ex_stage derives `div_busy = div_op && !div_done`);\n    added an `advance` input for the DONE -> IDLE hand-off.\n- `rtl/alu.sv`: one signed 33x33 multiply (`a_ext = {a_signed & a[31], a}`, etc.);\n  MUL = prod[31:0], MULH/MULHU/MULHSU = prod[63:32]. The four `/` `%` expressions\n  are gone from the non-ALTOPS branch (DIV-class ops hit `default: out = 0`).\n  ALTOPS branch unchanged.\n- `rtl/ex_stage.sv`: `div_op` (forced to 0 under ALTOPS), `divider` instance,\n  `ex_result = div_op ? div_result : alu_result`, new `div_busy` output.\n  EX/MEM update: stall -> hold; else div_busy -> bubble (`'0`); else normal capture.\n  RVFI `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` come from the divider's latched `a_q`/`b_q` for the DIV's own capture.\n  `write_data` still takes the forwarded `rs2` (only meaningful for stores; cosim only\n  compares mem_wdata under a non-zero wmask), so no extra mux sits on that timed path.\n- `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` / `rtl/core.sv`: `div_busy` input; `stall_if`/`stall_id` `|= div_busy`;\n  `flush_id` gated with `!div_busy`. `stall_ex_mem` / `hold_mem_wb` unchanged.\n- Tests: `test_alu.py` (DIV vectors removed, random sweep of all four MUL ops vs a Python\n  reference added, check that DIV ops fall through to 0); new `test_divider.py` (clocked,\n  all corner cases, operand-scramble-after-start, latency/hold, random); `test_pipeline.py`\n  (M-ext encoders, optional random ~22% bus stalls in `_run`, DIV->dependent ADD,\n  producer->DIV forwarding, back-to-back dependent divides, corner cases through the pipe,\n  load->DIV incl. DIV right behind an independent LW, 12-seed random-stall mix).\n\n## Verification (all run locally)\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench` clean; also clean with `-DRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- `pytest cores/bench/test/test_alu.py test_divider.py test_pipeline.py`: all pass\n  (14/14 divider, all pipeline tests incl. stall seeds).\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: `passed: true, elfs_tested: 2` (selftest + CoreMark\n  with/without stalls, CRCs OK).\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`, auto-selects\n  wrapper_si/checks_si for nret=1): **53 passed, 0 failed** (first attempt, no retries needed).\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (place option 0): **43.5 MHz** (baseline 5.44 MHz), 15 logic\n  levels, 28.3 ns worst path `u_rf regs -> u_id/u_ex/u_alu -> dmem BSRAM address`\n  (forwarding -> ALU/shared multiplier -> EX/MEM.alu_result). 2450 logic cells,\n  634 regs, 2 DSP (down from ~12.3K LUT4).\n\n## Notes / concerns\n\n- Remaining critical path is the forwarding mux -> ALU (shared multiplier) ->\n  `ex_result`/jump mux -> EX/MEM.alu_result (absorbed into the dmem BSRAM address register).\n  Further Fmax work would target that (e.g. pipelining/removing the extra `div_op` mux layer\n  or splitting the multiplier).\n- `make cosim` and `make formal` need `NRET=1` / no explicit checks cfg respectively for an\n  nret=1 core when invoked by hand (`make formal TARGET=bench` passes `formal/checks.cfg`\n  explicitly and so picks the dual-channel wrapper, which fails on a single-channel core\n  regardless of this change); the orchestrator selects the SI variants itself.\n- During the session one `Write` call targeted the main checkout's `cores/bench/test/` path by\n  mistake; it was denied by the permission layer and nothing was written there. The file was\n  then written in this worktree.\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 966, "cache_read_input_tokens": 171332, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 966}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5d95b1c8-e000-48b7-87d2-6f9a2fb11b69", "uuid": "4f2a275a-89a8-4edc-9762-658210830a63", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T08:59:44.966Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbF1yMSzfsKsKUry3SuM"}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_013qnkv2cqmrNnoBqynQtrvk", "type": "tool_result", "content": "File created successfully at: /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "5d95b1c8-e000-48b7-87d2-6f9a2fb11b69", "uuid": "da9bdf3a-f649-4975-be2c-90b68533e257", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T08:59:44.976Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "create", "filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-001-r1s0/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "content": "# Implementation notes — serial divider + shared multiplier (cores/bench)\n\n## What changed\n\n- `rtl/divider.sv` (new): radix-2 restoring serial divider, one-hot FSM\n  IDLE -> PREP -> RUN(32) -> FIX -> DONE.\n  - IDLE+`start` latches the raw post-forwarding `a`/`b` plus `is_signed`/`want_rem`\n    into `a_q`/`b_q`/flags (no negation, so the forwarding path is not lengthened).\n  - PREP computes |a|, |b|, clears the remainder, records `neg_q`/`neg_r`.\n    `neg_q` is suppressed when b == 0, so signed DIV by 0 stays all-ones.\n  - RUN: 33-bit shifted remainder `{rem, quo[31]}` vs |b| through one 34-bit\n    subtract; borrow selects restore/keep. (The hypothesis text wrote\n    `rem = {rem[30:0], q[31]}`; that would drop the top bit when |b| > 2^31, so\n    the shifted value is 33 bits wide and `rem` is 32 bits.)\n  - FIX: single shared negate of the selected (quotient|remainder) -> `quo` register.\n  - DONE: `done=1`, `result=quo`. Back to IDLE when `advance` (= `!stall_ex_mem`).\n  - 35 busy cycles + the DONE cycle per divide.\n  - Whole FSM under `ifndef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`; ALTOPS ties done/result/a_q/b_q to 0.\n  - Interface deviation: no `busy` output (ex_stage derives `div_busy = div_op && !div_done`);\n    added an `advance` input for the DONE -> IDLE hand-off.\n- `rtl/alu.sv`: one signed 33x33 multiply (`a_ext = {a_signed & a[31], a}`, etc.);\n  MUL = prod[31:0], MULH/MULHU/MULHSU = prod[63:32]. The four `/` `%` expressions\n  are gone from the non-ALTOPS branch (DIV-class ops hit `default: out = 0`).\n  ALTOPS branch unchanged.\n- `rtl/ex_stage.sv`: `div_op` (forced to 0 under ALTOPS), `divider` instance,\n  `ex_result = div_op ? div_result : alu_result`, new `div_busy` output.\n  EX/MEM update: stall -> hold; else div_busy -> bubble (`'0`); else normal capture.\n  RVFI `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` come from the divider's latched `a_q`/`b_q` for the DIV's own capture.\n  `write_data` still takes the forwarded `rs2` (only meaningful for stores; cosim only\n  compares mem_wdata under a non-zero wmask), so no extra mux sits on that timed path.\n- `rtl/hazard_unit.sv` / `rtl/core.sv`: `div_busy` input; `stall_if`/`stall_id` `|= div_busy`;\n  `flush_id` gated with `!div_busy`. `stall_ex_mem` / `hold_mem_wb` unchanged.\n- Tests: `test_alu.py` (DIV vectors removed, random sweep of all four MUL ops vs a Python\n  reference added, check that DIV ops fall through to 0); new `test_divider.py` (clocked,\n  all corner cases, operand-scramble-after-start, latency/hold, random); `test_pipeline.py`\n  (M-ext encoders, optional random ~22% bus stalls in `_run`, DIV->dependent ADD,\n  producer->DIV forwarding, back-to-back dependent divides, corner cases through the pipe,\n  load->DIV incl. DIV right behind an independent LW, 12-seed random-stall mix).\n\n## Verification (all run locally)\n\n- `make lint TARGET=bench` clean; also clean with `-DRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- `pytest cores/bench/test/test_alu.py test_divider.py test_pipeline.py`: all pass\n  (14/14 divider, all pipeline tests incl. stall seeds).\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: `passed: true, elfs_tested: 2` (selftest + CoreMark\n  with/without stalls, CRCs OK).\n- Formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`, auto-selects\n  wrapper_si/checks_si for nret=1): **53 passed, 0 failed** (first attempt, no retries needed).\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (place option 0): **43.5 MHz** (baseline 5.44 MHz), 15 logic\n  levels, 28.3 ns worst path `u_rf regs -> u_id/u_ex/u_alu -> dmem BSRAM address`\n  (forwarding -> ALU/shared multiplier -> EX/MEM.alu_result). 2450 logic cells,\n  634 regs, 2 DSP (down from ~12.3K LUT4).\n\n## Notes / concerns\n\n- Remaining critical path is the forwarding mux -> ALU (shared multiplier) ->\n  `ex_result`/jump mux -> EX/MEM.alu_result (absorbed into the dmem BSRAM address register).\n  Further Fmax work would target that (e.g. pipelining/removing the extra `div_op` mux layer\n  or splitting the multiplier).\n- `make cosim` and `make formal` need `NRET=1` / no explicit checks cfg respectively for an\n  nret=1 core when invoked by hand (`make formal TARGET=bench` passes `formal/checks.cfg`\n  explicitly and so picks the dual-channel wrapper, which fails on a single-channel core\n  regardless of this change); the orchestrator selects the SI variants itself.\n- During the session one `Write` call targeted the main checkout's `cores/bench/test/` path by\n  mistake; it was denied by the permission layer and nothing was written there. The file was\n  then written in this worktree.\n", "structuredPatch": [], "originalFile": null, "userModified": false}}
