{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbF3eK217XMqcpgsBEde","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The serial divider and shared multiplier are in, and every self-check passes. Local timing is 43.5 MHz against the 5.44 MHz baseline.\n\n- **Lint:** clean, with and without `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- **Unit and pipeline tests:** `test_alu.py`, the new `test_divider.py` (14 tests) and `test_pipeline.py` all pass. The new pipeline tests include 12 random-stall seeds.\n- **Cosim:** `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed on both ELFs, selftest and CoreMark, with and without stalls.\n- **Formal:** 53 passed, 0 failed on the first attempt, so no retries were needed.\n- **Timing:** `make timing TARGET=bench` at place option 0 gives 43.5 MHz with 15 logic levels. The worst path is 28.3 ns, from the regfile through the forwarding muxes and ALU to the dmem BSRAM address. The netlist is 2450 logic cells and 2 DSPs.\n\n`make formal TARGET=bench` and `make cosim TARGET=bench` fail on this nret=1 core when run by hand. They need `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` instead; the orchestrator picks the right variants itself.\n\nDeviations from the hypothesis:\n- **Remainder width:** the shifted remainder is 33 bits wide. The hypothesis's `{rem[30:0], q[31]}` would lose the top bit when the divisor is above 2^31.\n- **Divider interface:** it has no `busy` output; `ex_stage.sv` derives `div_busy = div_op && !div_done`. I added an `advance` input so the divider returns from DONE to IDLE.\n- **Store data:** `write_data` still takes the forwarded `rs2`. It only matters for stores, and cosim only checks it when a write mask is set.\n\nI mistakenly wrote `test_divider.py` to the main checkout's path first; the permission layer denied it, so nothing landed there, and I then wrote it in this worktree.\n\nThe notes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":383,"cache_read_input_tokens":175041,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":383},"output_tokens":765,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5d95b1c8-e000-48b7-87d2-6f9a2fb11b69","uuid":"27596b4a-7367-4e6d-85fd-75a77cf72d25","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:59:55.416Z","request_id":"req_011CfbF3dpFJqwbMRbRzcXcy"}
{"duration_api_ms": 500612, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "5d95b1c8-e000-48b7-87d2-6f9a2fb11b69", "total_cost_usd": 2.2950702000000005, "usage": {"input_tokens": 80, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 168019, "cache_read_input_tokens": 4735021, "output_tokens": 67583, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 29556}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 168019, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "inference_geo": "not_available", "iterations": [], "speed": "standard"}, "modelUsage": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": {"inputTokens": 80, "outputTokens": 67583, "cacheReadInputTokens": 4735021, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 168019, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 2.2950702000000005, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 29556, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [{"tool_name": "Write", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01BbMb9Ytb2es9v3dTRK2o8w", "tool_input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/test/test_divider.py", "content": "\"\"\"Unit tests for rtl/divider.sv — the radix-2 restoring serial divider.\n\nClocked: pulse `start` with the operands, then wait for `done`. The DIV /\nDIVU / REM / REMU vector set moved here from test_alu.py when the\ncombinational `/` and `%` left the ALU. Covers the RV32M corner cases\n(by-zero, INT_MIN/-1), back-to-back operations, operand latching (the\ninputs are scrambled right after `start`, exactly like the forwarding\nmuxes moving on while EX is parked) and random vectors against a Python\nreference.\n\nThe ALTOPS build ties done/result to 0; these tests only apply to the\nreal (non-ALTOPS) build used by cocotb/cosim.\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport random\n\nimport cocotb\nfrom cocotb.clock import Clock\nfrom cocotb.triggers import RisingEdge, Timer\n\nfrom _helpers import (\n    ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU,\n    run_cocotb,\n)\n\nMASK32 = 0xFFFFFFFF\nMAX_CYCLES = 64          # 1 (start) + PREP + 32 RUN + FIX + DONE = 36\n\n\ndef _s32(x):\n    x &= MASK32\n    return x - (1 << 32) if x & 0x80000000 else x\n\n\ndef ref(op, a, b):\n    \"\"\"RV32M reference semantics.\"\"\"\n    a &= MASK32\n    b &= MASK32\n    if op == ALU_DIVU:\n        return MASK32 if b == 0 else a // b\n    if op == ALU_REMU:\n        return a if b == 0 else a % b\n    sa, sb = _s32(a), _s32(b)\n    if op == ALU_DIV:\n        if b == 0:\n            return MASK32\n        if a == 0x80000000 and b == MASK32:\n            return 0x80000000\n        q = abs(sa) // abs(sb)\n        return (-q if (sa < 0) != (sb < 0) else q) & MASK32\n    if op == ALU_REM:\n        if b == 0:\n            return a\n        if a == 0x80000000 and b == MASK32:\n            return 0\n        r = abs(sa) % abs(sb)\n        return (-r if sa < 0 else r) & MASK32\n    raise ValueError(op)\n\n\nasync def _reset(dut):\n    cocotb.start_soon(Clock(dut.clock, 10, \"ns\").start())\n    dut.reset.value = 1\n    dut.start.value = 0\n    dut.advance.value = 1\n    dut.a.value = 0\n    dut.b.value = 0\n    dut.is_signed.value = 0\n    dut.want_rem.value = 0\n    for _ in range(3):\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    dut.reset.value = 0\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n\n\nasync def _divide(dut, op, a, b, scramble=True, hold_done=0):\n    \"\"\"Run one divide. Returns (result, a_q, b_q, cycles_until_done).\"\"\"\n    a &= MASK32\n    b &= MASK32\n    dut.a.value = a\n    dut.b.value = b\n    dut.is_signed.value = 1 if op in (ALU_DIV, ALU_REM) else 0\n    dut.want_rem.value = 1 if op in (ALU_REM, ALU_REMU) else 0\n    dut.start.value = 1\n    dut.advance.value = 1\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    dut.start.value = 0\n    if scramble:\n        # The forwarding muxes move on while EX is parked: the divider must\n        # have latched everything it needs at the start edge.\n        dut.a.value = (~a) & MASK32\n        dut.b.value = (b ^ 0x5A5A5A5A) & MASK32\n        dut.is_signed.value = 0 if op in (ALU_DIV, ALU_REM) else 1\n        dut.want_rem.value = 0 if op in (ALU_REM, ALU_REMU) else 1\n\n    cycles = 1\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    while int(dut.done.value) == 0:\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n        await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n        cycles += 1\n        assert cycles <= MAX_CYCLES, f\"divider never finished op={op} a={a:#x} b={b:#x}\"\n\n    result = int(dut.result.value)\n    a_q = int(dut.a_q.value)\n    b_q = int(dut.b_q.value)\n\n    # done must stay high with a stable result while the instruction is held\n    # in EX (advance low).\n    if hold_done:\n        dut.advance.value = 0\n        for _ in range(hold_done):\n            await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n            await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n            assert int(dut.done.value) == 1, \"done dropped while held\"\n            assert int(dut.result.value) == result, \"result changed while held\"\n        dut.advance.value = 1\n\n    # advance -> back to IDLE (done low) on the next cycle.\n    await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n    await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n    assert int(dut.done.value) == 0, \"done must clear after the instruction advances\"\n    return result, a_q, b_q, cycles\n\n\nasync def _check(dut, op, a, b, **kw):\n    result, a_q, b_q, _ = await _divide(dut, op, a, b, **kw)\n    exp = ref(op, a, b)\n    assert result == exp, (\n        f\"op={op} a=0x{a & MASK32:08x} b=0x{b & MASK32:08x} \"\n        f\"expected=0x{exp:08x} got=0x{result:08x}\"\n    )\n    assert a_q == a & MASK32 and b_q == b & MASK32, (\n        f\"latched operands wrong: a_q=0x{a_q:08x} b_q=0x{b_q:08x}\"\n    )\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def div_signed(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 10, 3)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFC, 2)       # -4/2 = -2\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 7, 0xFFFFFFFE)       # 7/-2 = -3 (trunc to 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFF9, 0xFFFFFFFE)  # -7/-2 = 3\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0, 5)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def div_by_zero(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 123, 0)              # all ones\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0, 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0)       # negative / 0: still all ones\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def div_overflow(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    # INT_MIN / -1 -> INT_MIN  (defined overflow per RV32IM)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 1)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 2)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def divu(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 2)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 100, 7)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)   # divisor > 2^31\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0xFFFFFFFE, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def divu_by_zero(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 42, 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0, 0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def rem_signed(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 10, 3)\n    # -10 % 3 trunc-to-zero: -10 = (-3)*3 + (-1) -> rem = -1 = 0xFFFFFFFF\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0xFFFFFFF6, 3)\n    # 10 % -3 trunc-to-zero: 10 = (-3)*(-3) + 1 -> rem = 1 (sign of dividend)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 10, 0xFFFFFFFD)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0xFFFFFFF6, 0xFFFFFFFD)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def rem_by_zero(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0xDEADBEEF, 0)       # dividend (negative)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 5, 0)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0x80000000, 0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def rem_overflow(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    # INT_MIN % -1 -> 0\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def remu(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REMU, 7, 3)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REMU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 0xFFFFFFFE)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REMU, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def remu_by_zero(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REMU, 0xCAFEBABE, 0)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def back_to_back_divides(dut):\n    \"\"\"Verify the FSM resets cleanly between consecutive divides — no\n    carry-over of operands or state from the previous op.\"\"\"\n    await _reset(dut)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 100, 7)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIVU, 0xFFFFFFFF, 2)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFC, 2)       # -4/2 = -2\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 10, 3)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REMU, 7, 3)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 5, 0)                # by-zero right after real ops\n    await _check(dut, ALU_REM, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n    await _check(dut, ALU_DIV, 0x80000000, 0xFFFFFFFF)\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def latency_and_hold(dut):\n    \"\"\"Fixed latency; done/result held stable while advance is low.\"\"\"\n    await _reset(dut)\n    _, _, _, cycles = await _divide(dut, ALU_DIVU, 1000, 7, hold_done=5)\n    assert cycles == 35, f\"expected 35 busy cycles before done, got {cycles}\"\n    _, _, _, cycles2 = await _divide(dut, ALU_DIV, 0xFFFFFFFF, 3, hold_done=2)\n    assert cycles2 == cycles\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def no_spurious_done(dut):\n    \"\"\"Without start the divider stays idle.\"\"\"\n    await _reset(dut)\n    for _ in range(40):\n        await RisingEdge(dut.clock)\n        await Timer(1, \"ns\")\n        assert int(dut.done.value) == 0\n\n\n@cocotb.test()\nasync def random_vectors(dut):\n    await _reset(dut)\n    rng = random.Random(0xD1F)\n    edges = [0, 1, 2, 3, MASK32, 0x80000000, 0x7FFFFFFF, 0x80000001, 0xFFFF0000, 0x0000FFFF]\n    for op in (ALU_DIV, ALU_DIVU, ALU_REM, ALU_REMU):\n        for a in edges:\n            for b in edges:\n                await _check(dut, op, a, b)\n        for _ in range(60):\n            # mix full-width, short divisors and short dividends\n            a = rng.getrandbits(rng.choice([8, 16, 31, 32]))\n            b = rng.getrandbits(rng.choice([4, 8, 16, 31, 32]))\n            if rng.random() < 0.25:\n                a = (-a) & MASK32\n            if rng.random() < 0.25:\n                b = (-b) & MASK32\n            await _check(dut, op, a, b)\n\n\ndef test_divider_runner():\n    \"\"\"pytest entry — runs every @cocotb.test() above under Verilator.\"\"\"\n    run_cocotb(toplevel=\"divider\",\n               sources=[\"core_pkg.sv\", \"divider.sv\"],\n               test_module=\"test_divider\")\n"}}], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 60, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "The serial divider and shared multiplier are in, and every self-check passes. Local timing is 43.5 MHz against the 5.44 MHz baseline.\n\n- **Lint:** clean, with and without `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- **Unit and pipeline tests:** `test_alu.py`, the new `test_divider.py` (14 tests) and `test_pipeline.py` all pass. The new pipeline tests include 12 random-stall seeds.\n- **Cosim:** `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed on both ELFs, selftest and CoreMark, with and without stalls.\n- **Formal:** 53 passed, 0 failed on the first attempt, so no retries were needed.\n- **Timing:** `make timing TARGET=bench` at place option 0 gives 43.5 MHz with 15 logic levels. The worst path is 28.3 ns, from the regfile through the forwarding muxes and ALU to the dmem BSRAM address. The netlist is 2450 logic cells and 2 DSPs.\n\n`make formal TARGET=bench` and `make cosim TARGET=bench` fail on this nret=1 core when run by hand. They need `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` and `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` instead; the orchestrator picks the right variants itself.\n\nDeviations from the hypothesis:\n- **Remainder width:** the shifted remainder is 33 bits wide. The hypothesis's `{rem[30:0], q[31]}` would lose the top bit when the divisor is above 2^31.\n- **Divider interface:** it has no `busy` output; `ex_stage.sv` derives `div_busy = div_op && !div_done`. I added an `advance` input so the divider returns from DONE to IDLE.\n- **Store data:** `write_data` still takes the forwarded `rs2`. It only matters for stores, and cosim only checks it when a write mask is set.\n\nI mistakenly wrote `test_divider.py` to the main checkout's path first; the permission layer denied it, so nothing landed there, and I then wrote it in this worktree.\n\nThe notes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.", "ttft_ms": 2457, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 519559, "uuid": "f6bded9d-a120-4b26-9680-693e3c442634", "ttft_stream_ms": 2330, "time_to_request_ms": 43, "first_content_frame_ms": 2330, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}

