{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01PdfYt6aLbJSizBsHkyHTfC", "type": "tool_result", "content": "The file /srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "21120814-0eb2-43dc-b8ac-434b292b2c39", "uuid": "99ec1eb9-eebd-429f-a182-ba1e29bc29a6", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:02:58.515Z", "tool_use_result": {"filePath": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r1s1/cores/bench/implementation_notes.md", "oldString": "(see below — filled in after the runs finished)", "newString": "- Local formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,\n  ALTOPS, nret=1 wrapper): **pass** — \"Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed\", first attempt,\n  no fix retries needed.\n- Local cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): **pass** — `passed: true,\n  elfs_tested: 2` (selftest + CoreMark with the random stall model).\n- `make timing TARGET=bench`: Fmax 46.48 MHz (see above).\n- Only files under cores/bench/rtl and cores/bench/test were touched.", "originalFile": "# Implementation notes — multi-cycle MUL/DIV/REM unit (cores/bench)\n\n## What changed\n\n- **rtl/muldiv.sv (new)**: multi-cycle RV32M unit, interface\n  `clock/reset/start/hold/op/a/b -> done/result/a_lat/b_lat`.\n  - While IDLE it samples `op/a/b` into its own registers every cycle and\n    leaves IDLE on the first cycle `start` is high (`start` may stay high while\n    busy; ignored outside IDLE).\n  - MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU: one shared signed 33x33 multiplier from four 16/17-bit\n    partial products (Al*Bl, Al*Bh, Ah*Bl, Ah*Bh). Stage MUL1 registers the four\n    partial products (one DSP each, no adder in the path), stage MUL2 registers the\n    64-bit three-operand sum and the hi/lo select. DONE = start cycle + 3\n    (i.e. 3 stall cycles, M-op leaves EX in the 4th).\n  - DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU: PREP (abs values, sign flags) -> 32 x RUN (restoring\n    shift/compare/subtract, all registered) -> FIX (negate selected result) -> DONE.\n    DONE = start cycle + 35. Div-by-zero: quotient all ones (negate suppressed when\n    b==0), remainder = dividend. INT_MIN/-1 falls out naturally.\n  - `done` is `state[3]` (a flop output) so the stall logic sees no decode.\n- **rtl/alu.sv**: the real (non-ALTOPS) branch no longer contains `*`, `/`, `%`\n  (M ops fall to `default -> 0`). The `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` stand-ins are\n  unchanged byte-for-byte.\n- **rtl/ex_stage.sv**: instantiates `muldiv`; `is_md_op = alu_op >= ALU_MUL`,\n  `md_busy = is_md_op && !md_done`, `start = is_md_op && !stall`, `hold = stall`.\n  New output `md_busy`. EX/MEM captures a bubble (`reg_q <= '0`) on\n  `md_busy`, with the dmem stall (`stall`) still taking priority (hold). In the DONE\n  cycle `alu_result <= md_result`, and `rs1_val/rs2_val/write_data` come from the\n  latched operands (RVFI rs1_rdata/rs2_rdata). Under `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`,\n  `is_md_op = 0`, `md_busy = 0` and the muldiv instance is not elaborated, so the\n  formal build never stalls.\n- **rtl/hazard_unit.sv**: new `md_busy` input OR-ed into `stall_if` and `stall_id`.\n  `flush_*`, `stall_ex_mem`, `hold_mem_wb` unchanged (an M-op in EX is neither a\n  load nor a redirect, so `load_use`/`redirect` are 0 while it waits).\n- **rtl/core.sv**: wires `ex_stage.md_busy -> hazard_unit.md_busy`.\n- **test/test_alu.py**: removed the combinational M-extension vectors (and the\n  `_check_div` helper); base-ISA ALU tests stay.\n- **test/test_muldiv.py (new)**: cocotb test for `muldiv.sv` — per op (8 ops) >= 30\n  exact-bit vectors against a Python RV32M model (directed corners incl. x/0,\n  INT_MIN/-1, signed corners, corner cross-product, random), explicit spec vectors\n  independent of the model, back-to-back mixed ops, `hold` (dmem-stall-at-DONE)\n  keeping `done`/result/latched operands, IDLE sampling without `start`, and latency\n  bounds (mul <= 6, div <= 40 cycles).\n\n## Deviations from the hypothesis text\n\n- Mul latency is 3 stall cycles (MUL1 partial products, MUL2 sum, then DONE), the\n  upper end of the 2-3 suggested. `make timing` showed the multiplier stages are not\n  critical (see below); I did not try to shave a stage because the worst path is\n  elsewhere and a multiply is <1% of CoreMark instructions.\n- Extra `hold` input on `muldiv` (= `stall_ex_mem`) so DONE is held with the result\n  stable if a dmem stall coincides with DONE (in practice EX/MEM holds a bubble from\n  the start cycle on, so this cannot actually happen in the pipeline, but it is\n  handled).\n- `write_data` (store data / RVFI mem_wdata replication) also uses the latched rs2 in\n  the DONE cycle so the non-store M-op EX/MEM payload matches the baseline.\n\n## Results (local)\n\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall -Wno-MULTITOP` is clean, with and without\n  `-DRISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`.\n- `pytest cores/bench/test/test_muldiv.py test_alu.py`: 13 muldiv tests + ALU tests pass.\n  Measured latencies: MUL* done 3 cycles after start, DIV*/REM* 35.\n- `make timing TARGET=bench` (placement option 0): **Fmax 46.48 MHz** (baseline 5.44),\n  21 logic levels, 2 DSPs, 2436 logic cells, 665 registers. Worst path 26.8 ns is\n  the ordinary regfile/forward -> redirect/hazard -> PC / ID-EX path\n  (`u_rf -> u_id -> u_ex -> u_if -> u_hazard -> u_id/u_if`), no multiplier/divider path.\n\n## Concerns / notes\n\n- `make formal-deep` (no ALTOPS) now sees real multi-cycle M ops: a divide takes\n  ~36 cycles, longer than the deep BMC depth, so the per-insn M-op checks there\n  can no longer exhibit a retirement within the bound. M-ext arithmetic is covered by\n  test_muldiv.py + cosim instead (invariant 5b).\n- Operand latching relies on ID/EX holding the M-op (stall_id=1) so `in.ctrl.alu_op`\n  stays stable while busy; `op` is only consumed by muldiv in the start cycle plus the\n  `f_*` flags it latches then.\n- Run `make formal` as `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`\n  (nret auto-detect); `make formal TARGET=bench` passes an explicit checks.cfg and\n  selects the NRET=2 wrapper, which fails on this nret=1 core (`_1` ports).\n\n## Formal / cosim status\n\n(see below — filled in after the runs finished)\n", "structuredPatch": [{"oldStart": 80, "oldLines": 4, "newStart": 80, "newLines": 10, "lines": [" ", " ## Formal / cosim status", " ", "-(see below — filled in after the runs finished)", "+- Local formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`,", "+  ALTOPS, nret=1 wrapper): **pass** — \"Formal: 53 passed, 0 failed\", first attempt,", "+  no fix retries needed.", "+- Local cosim (`NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`): **pass** — `passed: true,", "+  elfs_tested: 2` (selftest + CoreMark with the random stall model).", "+- `make timing TARGET=bench`: Fmax 46.48 MHz (see above).", "+- Only files under cores/bench/rtl and cores/bench/test were touched."]}], "userModified": false, "replaceAll": false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbFHeWZt6CQ1TaFr59f5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The multi-cycle MUL/DIV/REM unit is in, and all my local checks pass. `make timing TARGET=bench` gives Fmax **46.48 MHz** (placement option 0), up from the 5.44 MHz baseline.\n\n- **Timing:** the worst path is now 26.8 ns, 21 logic levels, on the register-file/forward → redirect/hazard → PC / ID-EX route, with no multiplier or divider path. The build uses 2 DSPs, 2436 logic cells and 665 registers. I only ran placement option 0, not the median over three options.\n- **Formal:** 53 passed, 0 failed on the first attempt, so no fix retries were needed.\n- **Cosim:** passed on both ELFs, selftest and CoreMark under the random stall model.\n- **Lint and tests:** lint is clean with and without `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS`. All 13 tests in the new `test_muldiv.py` pass, plus the trimmed `test_alu.py`.\n\n**Latency:** a multiply takes 3 stall cycles. A divide or remainder takes 35.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `muldiv.sv` is new.\n- `alu.sv` no longer has `*`, `/` or `%` in the real build. The ALTOPS stand-ins are untouched.\n- `ex_stage.sv` stalls EX for M-ops and takes the result and RVFI operands from the unit. With ALTOPS defined the stall path and the unit are compiled out.\n- `hazard_unit.sv` and `core.sv` carry the new `md_busy` stall.\n- `test_alu.py` no longer has the M-extension vectors.\n\n**Deviations:**\n- `muldiv` has an extra `hold` input, tied to the dmem stall, so a result stays valid if a stall coincides with DONE. In this pipeline that coincidence can't actually happen.\n- The store-data register also takes the latched rs2 in the DONE cycle, so the payload for M-ops matches the baseline.\n\n**Concerns:**\n- **Formal gate:** `make formal TARGET=bench` fails on this nret=1 core, because it passes an explicit checks file and picks the nret=2 wrapper. Run `RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh` instead.\n- **`formal-deep`:** a divide now takes about 36 cycles, longer than the deep BMC depth. The per-instruction M-op checks there probably can't show a retirement within the bound. I did not run it. Arithmetic correctness rests on `test_muldiv.py` and cosim.\n\nThese are also recorded in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":149850,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":615},"output_tokens":846,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"21120814-0eb2-43dc-b8ac-434b292b2c39","uuid":"f8578f74-52e0-47cf-931c-326fcd92dbb9","timestamp":"2026-10-01T09:03:06.103Z","request_id":"req_011CfbFHe2nWeTtUMN2oaq6M"}
