{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbEs7u9La2NejECfZFAU", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01A3pHyF6szTEFdqGXwrWQAe", "name": "Bash", "input": {"command": "cat > cores/bench/implementation_notes.md <<'EOF'\n# Fetch-stage predecode predictor (JAL always-taken + 256x2b bimodal)\n\n## What changed (cores/bench/rtl only)\n- `core_pkg.sv`: `if_id_t` and `id_ex_t` gain `pred_taken` (1b) and `pred_cnt` (2b).\n- `if_stage.sv`: predecodes `imem_data` (IF/ID are merged, so it is available in the same\n  cycle as `imem_addr = pc`).\n  - JAL -> always predicted taken, target = pc + J-imm.\n  - BRANCH -> taken iff MSB of `bht[pc[9:2]]` (256 x 2b saturating counters, un-reset array,\n    async read / sync write), target = pc + B-imm.\n  - JALR / everything else -> pc+4.\n  - One shared adder `pc + (is_jal ? jal_imm : br_imm)`; `next_pc = pred_taken ? target : pc+4`.\n    `redirect` still has priority over everything and `stall` still holds the PC.\n  - A prediction is only made if `target[1:0] == 0` (applies to JAL too), so `imem_addr` is\n    always aligned even for symbolic streams.\n  - `out.pred_taken` is masked with `!(flush || redirect)`.\n  - Table write port driven from EX (`train_en/idx/taken/cnt`).\n- `id_stage.sv`: latches `pred_taken`/`pred_cnt` into ID/EX (zero on reset/flush via the existing `'0`).\n- `ex_stage.sv`: resolved next PC computed once (`resolved_npc`); `redirect = in.valid &&\n  (resolved_taken != in.pred_taken)`, `redirect_target = resolved_npc`; `reg_q.pc_next` uses the\n  same `resolved_npc` (resolved outcome, never the prediction, so RVFI pc_wdata and the\n  misalign-trap behaviour are unchanged). Train strobe: `in.valid && is_branch && !stall`.\n- `core.sv`: wires the 4 train signals EX -> IF. No top-level IO change.\n\n## Deviations from the hypothesis text\n1. **No `pred_target` carried in ID/EX and no 32-bit resolved-vs-predicted compare.** For JAL and\n   conditional branches the predicted target is `pc + imm` from the same instruction word that EX\n   recomputes (`in.pc + in.imm`, `imm_gen` uses identical J/B formulas), so when both predicted\n   and actual are \"taken\" the targets are identical by construction. Mismatch therefore reduces to\n   `resolved_taken != pred_taken`. This covers: JALR (never predicted, redirects when it jumps),\n   misaligned-target traps (resolved = pc+4, no redirect, same as baseline), illegal branch funct3\n   2/3 (predicted taken from opcode alone but `is_branch=0` in EX -> mismatch -> redirect to pc+4),\n   and aliasing/garbage table contents. Saves 32 flops and a 32-bit comparator on the redirect path.\n2. **Counter read at fetch rides down the pipe (`pred_cnt`)** and the new value is computed from it\n   at train time, instead of a second read port on the table. Only difference vs. a re-read: if the\n   same entry is trained by the instruction one slot ahead, the update uses the value read before\n   that update (rare, harmless for correctness).\n3. JAL also gets the aligned-target gate (hypothesis only gated branches).\n\n## Results\n- Local formal (`RTL_DIR=cores/bench/rtl CORE_NAME=bench bash formal/run_all.sh`): 53 passed, 0 failed.\n- `verilator --lint-only -Wall`: clean.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench`: passed (selftest + CoreMark CRCs, with/without stalls).\n- CoreMark `--bench --istall --dstall`: bracketed cycles 4,193,173 (start 14,998 / stop 4,208,171)\n  vs baseline 4,491,485 => ~6.6% fewer cycles (~+7.1% iterations/cycle), matching the ~6.7% replay estimate.\n- `make timing` was NOT run (30 min budget). Expected Fmax unchanged: new logic (one 32b adder +\n  mux in IF, one XOR in the redirect path, 256x2 LUT-RAM read) is far shorter than the ~199 ns ALU path.\n\n## Concerns\n- The bimodal table is un-reset; synthesis should map it to LUT-RAM (async read). If the vendor flow\n  instead builds 512 FFs + 256:1 muxes it is still tiny vs. the ALU path, but LUT/FF count rises.\n- Power-up counters are 0 (strongly not-taken) in 2-state simulation, i.e. the same as baseline until trained.\nEOF\n(time pytest -q cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py) 2>&1 | tail -8", "description": "Write implementation notes and run pipeline unit tests", "timeout": 300000}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1150, "cache_read_input_tokens": 102860, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1150}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "a17846b7-0d47-40a4-b7f7-09328e3ceaf3", "uuid": "47759d00-7146-40f3-a0af-dc1ff2c59b4d", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T08:57:41.555Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbEs7Wpk7UdbfbTpQnzo"}
