{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbEwBhhxFQoRBnFk4r5v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fetch-stage predictor is in `cores/bench/rtl/` and cuts CoreMark cycles by about 6.6% in local runs. I did not run `make timing`, so the Gowin Fmax is unmeasured.\n\n- **Cycles:** CoreMark with `--istall --dstall` now takes 4,193,173 bracketed cycles, against the 4,491,485 you quoted for the baseline. That is roughly +7.1% iterations per cycle, in line with your replay estimate.\n- **Checks:** Local formal passed 53 of 53 with 0 failed. `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed, including the CoreMark CRCs. Verilator lint is clean and all 13 pipeline cocotb tests pass.\n\nJAL is always predicted taken, and conditional branches use a 256-entry 2-bit bimodal table indexed by `pc[9:2]`. EX checks every prediction and redirects on a mismatch, so `pc_next` and the RVFI output still come from the resolved outcome. The changes are in `if_stage.sv`, `core_pkg.sv`, `id_stage.sv`, `ex_stage.sv` and `core.sv`.\n\nThree places where I deviated from the hypothesis:\n- **No carried target or 32-bit compare:** I don't carry `pred_target` through ID/EX and don't compare resolved and predicted next PC. For JAL and branches the predicted target is the same `pc + imm` that EX recomputes, so a mismatch is just \"taken\" versus \"not taken\". This also covers JALR, misaligned targets, and illegal branch encodings (funct3 2 or 3).\n- **Counter rides the pipe:** The counter read at fetch travels down the pipe (`pred_cnt`), and training computes the new value from it. The table therefore needs only one read port; the cost is a slightly stale update if the same entry is trained one slot earlier.\n- **JAL alignment gate:** JAL also gets the aligned-target gate, so `imem_addr` stays aligned.\n\nI added two tests to `cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py`: one checks that a JAL target retires with no bubble, the other runs a BNE loop and checks the exact retirement sequence. The notes are in `cores/bench/implementation_notes.md`.\n\nThe un-reset table should map to LUT-RAM; if the vendor flow builds flops and muxes instead, LUT and FF counts rise slightly, but it stays well below the ALU path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":435,"cache_read_input_tokens":110474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":435},"output_tokens":804,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a17846b7-0d47-40a4-b7f7-09328e3ceaf3","uuid":"9da90956-98a9-4dfa-b6c7-ff7d19e6edea","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:58:27.911Z","request_id":"req_011CfbEwBCgxugLZYEhJA9su"}
