{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01WgUkGfeWbmaZzJR1tfaciE", "type": "tool_result", "content": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-bc9e0eb\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T08:48:19.219187Z\", \"round_id\": 0, \"slot\": 0}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261001-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Replace combinational DIV/REM array with a 34-cycle serial divider; share one multiplier\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"motivation\": \"The baseline closes timing at only 5.44 MHz. The reported worst path is 199.8 ns\\nwith 156 logic cells / ~150 logic levels, going MEM/WB.rd -> forward_unit -> ex_stage\\n-> alu -> EX/MEM.alu_result (which Gowin absorbs into the dmem BSRAM address register).\\nA path that deep can only be the four combinational 32-bit `/` and `%` array dividers\\nin alu.sv (signed/unsigned quotient and remainder). They also explain the 12.3K LUT4\\ncount. The three separate 64-bit multipliers (mul_ss, mul_uu, mul_su) add area and\\nan extra operand-mux layer on top of that. Every other path in this 5-stage core\\n(forwarding mux -> adder -> redirect, BSRAM read -> load align) is an order of\\nmagnitude shorter. CoreMark's timed region executes essentially no DIV/REM\\n(the compiler turns constant divisions into multiply-high at -O3, and the printf/\\nsetup code that divides sits outside the start/stop MMIO markers), so an\\niterative divider costs ~0 cycles of IPC while removing the dominant critical path.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The baseline c\n…[1333 of 4405 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:59a783841b955706]…\nt path 199.8 ns, 156 logic cells, 150 logic\\nlevels): the critical path runs forwarding select -> EX operand mux ->\\nu_alu -> dmem address, and it is dominated by the purely combinational\\n32-bit `/` and `%` (signed + unsigned) plus three 32x32 multipliers that\\nalu.sv instantiates and muxes into the single-cycle ALU result. Every other\\npath in this 5-stage core (fwd mux -> 32-bit add -> EX/MEM / BSRAM address,\\nfwd -> 32-bit branch compare -> redi\nhyp-20261001-003-r1s2.yaml\nname: bench\ndescription: Frozen LLM-benchmark fixture core. Identical RTL to baseline at the bench-fixture-v1\n  freeze point. The benchmark matrix clones from the bench-fixture-v1 orphan branch\n  and operates only on this directory.\nisa: rv32im\nnret: 1\ntarget_fpga: tang-nano-20k\ntargets:\n  fmax_mhz: 135\n  lut4: 10000\n  coremark_iter_s: 300\n  coremark_per_mhz: 2.2\ncurrent:\n  fmax_mhz: 47.258\n  lut4: 2450\n  ff: 634\n  coremark_iter_s: 2.0e-06\n  coremark_per_mhz: 0.0\n  source_id: hyp-20261001-001-r1s0\n  updated: '2026-10-01T09:04:37.351062Z'", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "8476c0cc-0f21-40dc-9df3-aa41adadf196", "uuid": "a57be25b-298f-4132-bbbd-f2a7b8a26391", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T09:05:11.230Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-bc9e0eb\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 4