{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbEJQwQSZ21ZDj5cPLzV", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_014cYSUs9fBEzU57h7zABoLj", "name": "Write", "input": {"file_path": "/srv/hwebench/clones/claude-sonnet-5-5_xhigh-v2-rep1/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261001-002-r1s1-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r1s1.yaml", "content": "id: hyp-20261001-002-r1s1\ntitle: \"Move MUL/DIV/REM out of the combinational ALU into a multi-cycle EX-stall muldiv unit\"\ncategory: structural\nmotivation: |\n  Baseline Fmax is 5.44 MHz (worst path 199.8 ns, 156 logic cells, 150 logic\n  levels): the critical path runs forwarding select -> EX operand mux ->\n  u_alu -> dmem address, and it is dominated by the purely combinational\n  32-bit `/` and `%` (signed + unsigned) plus three 32x32 multipliers that\n  alu.sv instantiates and muxes into the single-cycle ALU result. Every other\n  path in this 5-stage core (fwd mux -> 32-bit add -> EX/MEM / BSRAM address,\n  fwd -> 32-bit branch compare -> redirect -> PC) is only ~10-14 LUT levels,\n  i.e. roughly 20-30 ns. Fitness = iter/cycle x Fmax, and CoreMark executes\n  almost no divides inside the timed region and only ~0.4-1% multiplies (the\n  9x9 matrix kernels), so the single-cycle M-extension buys essentially no\n  IPC while costing ~7x in clock period and ~6-8k LUT4 of area.\nhypothesis: |\n  Make M-extension ops multi-cycle and remove them from the combinational\n  ALU. Concretely:\n\n  1. New rtl/muldiv.sv with a clock/reset/start/op/a/b -> done/result\n     interface. It latches the (post-forward) operands, then:\n       - MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU: ONE shared signed 33x33 multiplier (operands\n         sign- or zero-extended to 33 bits per op) built as explicit\n         16/17-bit partial products (maps to Gowin 18x18 DSPs) with a register\n         after the partial products and a register after the 64-bit sum, so\n         no path contains more than one DSP or one wide adder. Result mux\n         picks [31:0] or [63:32]. 2-3 extra EX cycles per multiply (use the\n         fewest stages that `make timing` shows are not critical).\n       - DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU: iterative restoring divider, 1 bit/cycle (~34-36\n         cycles): PREP (take absolute values, record signs), 32 shift/compare/\n         subtract iterations on registered rem/quo/divisor, FIX (negate\n         quotient if signs differ and divisor != 0, negate remainder if\n         dividend negative). Divide-by-zero: quotient = all ones, remainder =\n         dividend (suppress the quotient negate when b==0). INT_MIN/-1 falls\n         out naturally (|INT_MIN|/1 with same signs -> 0x80000000, rem 0).\n         All divider state is register-to-register, so none of it touches the\n         forwarding/ALU critical path.\n\n  2. EX-stage stall handling (ex_stage.sv + hazard_unit.sv + core.sv).\n     is_md_op = in.ctrl.alu_op >= ALU_MUL (decoder only emits >= 11 for legal\n     M ops; bubbles/NOPs decode to ADD). md_busy = is_md_op && !md_done.\n       - While md_busy: stall_if = 1 and stall_id = 1 (hold PC and ID/EX, flush_id\n         stays 0 -- an M-op in EX is neither a load nor a redirect, so\n         load_use and redirect are both 0), and the EX/MEM register captures a\n         bubble (reg_q <= '0 => valid=0, reg_write=0, no mem op) UNLESS\n         stall_ex_mem (dmem stall) is asserted, in which case EX/MEM simply\n         holds (existing behaviour wins).\n       - Operand capture: while the muldiv unit is IDLE it samples the\n         forwarded rs1/rs2 every cycle; it only leaves IDLE on the first\n         cycle where is_md_op && !stall_ex_mem. After that the forwarding\n         muxes see bubbles / retired producers, so ONLY the latched operands\n         may be used. In the final (DONE) cycle, EX/MEM.rs1_val / rs2_val\n         (RVFI rs1_rdata / rs2_rdata, checked by cosim and riscv-formal) must\n         come from the latched operands, and EX/MEM.alu_result <= md_result.\n       - Leave condition: M-op leaves EX in the DONE cycle when\n         !stall_ex_mem; the unit returns to IDLE the following cycle. If a\n         dmem stall coincides with DONE, stay in DONE (result held).\n       - Dependent consumers need no extra stall: the M-op's result is in\n         EX/MEM.alu_result like any ALU op and is forwarded normally.\n\n  3. ALTOPS / formal: keep the `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS branch exactly as\n     today (combinational XOR-of-add/sub stand-ins in alu.sv) and under\n     ALTOPS force is_md_op = 0 so the formal build never stalls; the real\n     branch of alu.sv drops the mul/div expressions (default -> 0, M-op\n     result comes from muldiv). This preserves invariant 5b: the real\n     arithmetic is covered by cosim + a new cocotb test_muldiv.py (>=30\n     vectors per M op incl. div-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, signed corner cases)\n     because test_alu.py's combinational M-ext vectors no longer apply to\n     alu.sv and must be removed from it.\n\n  Expected effect: the 150-level ALU path disappears; the new critical path\n  is the ordinary forward -> add/compare -> redirect/EX-MEM/BSRAM-address\n  path (~20-30 ns), so Fmax should rise from ~5.4 MHz to roughly 30-45 MHz.\n  Cycle count rises by only ~1-3% (a few thousand multiplies x 2-3 stall\n  cycles out of ~449k cycles/iteration; divides are not in the timed loop in\n  any quantity), and LUT4 drops substantially because the combinational\n  divider and 2 of 3 wide multipliers vanish. Net fitness gain several x,\n  well beyond the 4.6% acceptance threshold (schema caps the reported delta\n  at +50).\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 50\n  confidence: high\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/muldiv.sv\n    description: \"New module: multi-cycle M-extension unit. Latch operands while IDLE, shared signed 33x33 pipelined multiplier (explicit 16/17-bit partial products, registered stages) for MUL/MULH/MULHU/MULHSU, and iterative 1-bit/cycle restoring divider (PREP/RUN/FIX) for DIV/DIVU/REM/REMU with RV32M div-by-zero and INT_MIN/-1 semantics. Exposes start/op/a/b, done, result, and the latched operands (for RVFI).\"\n  - file: rtl/alu.sv\n    description: \"Remove the 64-bit multiplies and `/` `%` from the real (non-ALTOPS) branch so no wide arithmetic is in the single-cycle ALU path; M ops fall to default (0). Keep the `ifdef RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS substitutions byte-for-byte.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Instantiate muldiv; compute is_md_op/md_busy (forced 0 under ALTOPS); output md_busy; on md_busy && !stall capture a bubble into EX/MEM; use md_result as alu_result and latched operands as rs1_val/rs2_val in the DONE cycle.\"\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \"Add md_busy input; OR it into stall_if and stall_id (hold PC and ID/EX). flush_id/flush_if/stall_ex_mem/hold_mem_wb semantics unchanged; dmem_stall keeps priority.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the new ex_stage md_busy output into hazard_unit.\"\n  - file: test/test_alu.py\n    description: \"Drop the combinational M-extension vectors (mul/mulh/mulhu/mulhsu/div/divu/rem/remu) from the ALU unit test; base-ISA ALU ops stay.\"\n  - file: test/test_muldiv.py\n    description: \"New cocotb test for muldiv.sv: start/done handshake, >=30 exact-bit vectors per M op including divide-by-zero, INT_MIN/-1, negative operands, and back-to-back operations; checks bounded latency.\"\n"}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7918, "cache_read_input_tokens": 56589, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7918}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "0a5c2042-ac1e-4a41-9f1e-b6