{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbEQGDhYsisk7drn8s5h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the hypothesis to `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-002-r1s1.yaml`. It passes `schemas/hypothesis.schema.json`. I didn't run simulation or `make timing`, so the Fmax estimate below comes from reasoning about the paths, not a measurement.\n\n**What it proposes:** move MUL/DIV/REM out of the combinational ALU into a new multi-cycle `rtl/muldiv.sv`, with the EX stage stalling while it runs.\n\n**Why:** Fmax is 5.44 MHz because the worst path is about 200 ns through the ALU. That path is dominated by the combinational 32-bit `/` and `%` and the three 32x32 multipliers. The other EX paths look like roughly 20–30 ns, so removing the ALU path should take Fmax to about 30–45 MHz. CoreMark has almost no divides in the timed region and under 1% multiplies, so the extra cycles should cost only about 1–3%.\n\n**Design:**\n- **Multiplier:** one shared 33x33 signed multiplier built from partial products on the DSPs. It has registers after the partial products and after the sum, adding 2–3 EX cycles per multiply.\n- **Divider:** an iterative 1-bit-per-cycle restoring divider of about 34–36 cycles. It covers divide-by-zero and `INT_MIN / -1`.\n- **Stall handling:**\n  - While the unit is busy, the PC and ID/EX hold and EX/MEM takes a bubble. A dmem stall still takes priority over the bubble.\n  - The unit latches the forwarded operands on its first non-stalled cycle. The final cycle takes `rs1_val`/`rs2_val` from those latched copies so the RVFI values stay correct.\n  - The ALTOPS branch of `alu.sv` is unchanged, and under ALTOPS the stall is forced off so the formal build never waits.\n- **Tests:** the combinational M-ext vectors move out of `test_alu.py` into a new `test_muldiv.py`, which keeps invariant 5b covered.\n\n`expected_impact` is `fitness_delta_pct: 50` with `high` confidence. The schema caps the delta at +50, so the real expected gain is several times higher."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":523,"cache_read_input_tokens":74450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":523},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0a5c2042-ac1e-4a41-9f1e-b6c1e473d3ae","uuid":"1d2f7ce1-6faa-4af0-b156-4bcd38e2cb72","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:51:28.046Z","request_id":"req_011CfbEQFmQyjyehn4YyKpHX"}
