{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfbETXYHQ1mLGfu9gCdb7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote the hypothesis to `cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261001-003-r1s2.yaml`. It passes the schema check. I haven't implemented it or run synthesis, so the +6% is an estimate from an offline replay.\n\n**The proposal:** a fetch-stage predictor, with no BTB, that reads the fetched instruction directly. This works because IF and ID are merged, so `imem_data` is available in the same cycle as `pc`.\n- **JAL:** always predicted taken, with the target computed as `pc + imm` in IF.\n- **Conditional branches:** a 256-entry table of 2-bit counters indexed by `pc[9:2]`, trained from EX. The target is `pc + imm`.\n- **JALR and everything else:** predicted not-taken, as today.\n- **Verification in EX:** the existing resolved next PC is compared with the predicted one, and `redirect` fires on a mismatch. A mispredict costs the same one bubble a taken branch costs today. RVFI `pc_wdata` and the misalign traps behave as in the baseline.\n\n**Why I expect it to help:** I ran the CoreMark binary on the reference ISS, replayed its 2.94M-instruction control-flow trace, and ran the predictor on that.\n- **Baseline cost:** taken redirects happen 0.122 times per instruction. That is about 8% of cycles, at roughly 1.53 CPI (4,491,485 cycles for 10 iterations).\n- **Predictor result:** JALs are always correct, conditional branches are about 87% accurate, and about 84% of redirect bubbles go away. That is roughly 6.7% fewer cycles.\n- **Adjustment:** I discounted that a bit for redirects that already overlap a dmem stall, which gives my +6%. That is above the 4.6% acceptance bar, but not by a wide margin.\n- **Fmax:** the 199 ns ALU path sets Fmax and everything else has about 180 ns of slack. The new adder, mux and 32-bit compare should not move it.\n\nI left out a return-address stack and gshare. In the replay they add only about 0.3% each, and they would make the change larger and riskier.\n\nThe five files to change are `rtl/core_pkg.sv`, `rtl/if_stage.sv`, `rtl/id_stage.sv`, `rtl/ex_stage.sv` and `rtl/core.sv`. I removed the `coremark.elf` I built for tracing, so the worktree is clean."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3540,"cache_read_input_tokens":82672,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3540},"output_tokens":797,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b1e97de-d89b-4a8a-930a-7e570581fb2d","uuid":"f73a8cc7-6f42-4b6c-ba44-a3516cab47f5","timestamp":"2026-10-01T08:52:12.794Z","request_id":"req_011CfbETXACvgCTsHTf8q15C"}
